[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0)--(7,0);
\foreach \x in {0,3.5,7} {\draw (\x,-0.12)--(\x,0.12);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.15) {$0$};
\node[below] at (3.5,-0.15) {$\frac{1}{2}$};
\node[below] at (7,-0.15) {$1$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0.7,1.0)--(0.7,0.2);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (3.5,1.0)--(3.5,0.2);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (6.3,1.0)--(6.3,0.2);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (7,1.0)--(7,0.2);
\node at (0.7,1.3) {$A$};
\node at (3.5,1.3) {$B$};
\node at (6.3,1.3) {$C$};
\node at (7,1.3) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Four probabilities are marked on the scale. Which arrow shows the probability of an event that is unlikely, but not impossible?
